## Architecture decisions carried (from the review, pending final lock on answers)

- Name: **Inkwell** (committed, single name, no internal/external split).
- Store: SQLite canonical (pending L3 confirm), markdown daily-page export to `~/OneDrive/04_Inkwell/{YYYY-MM-DD}.md` as a view.
- GitHub-backed store / mirror: **killed entirely.** Capture latency and privacy.
- Voice framing: "Telegram voice note → Pulse → store," not "ElevenLabs flow."
- Views in MVP: **Today, Everything** (two, not three — Inbox/Backlog is a filter, not a view).

## MVP scope (the two-week bake-off build)

In:
- SQLite store at `~/.claude/PAI/MEMORY/INKWELL/inkwell.db`.
- CLI: `ink add "..."`, `ink today`, `ink done <id>`, `ink mv <id> today`.
- Telegram bot: text capture (+ voice-note capture pending L1).
- Daily Telegram check-in at 17:00 Melbourne: "What got done? Anything to roll?" Agent updates the store on Nick's reply.
- Daily markdown export to OneDrive (the notebook-page artefact).
- Project allocation defaults to "inbox"; agent guesses project from title and proposes on capture (one-tap accept).

Out of MVP: web app, mobile PWA, time blocks, Pulse widget, calendar integration, recurring tasks, Telos rollup, backlog-hygiene automation.

